1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,000
A manufacturing business can have skilled

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,340
engineers, good machines,

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,220
and suppliers it trusts.

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,060
And still, one person ends up holding it

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,200
all together.

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,700
When the answers live in phone calls,

7
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,260
spreadsheets and memory,

8
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,840
every question comes back to the owner.

9
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,500
Verity gives the work a record of its own.

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,540
So the answer is already there.

11
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:38,540
It starts with an enquiry.

12
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,340
A water board needs two booster pump

13
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:43,380
skids, built to its own specification.

14
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:46,740
The quote goes through revisions.

15
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,480
When the customer approves one,

16
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:50,520
its value is fixed on the job,

17
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:52,360
whatever changes later.

18
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:57,900
Approval opens the project.

19
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,060
Tasks wait for the work they depend on,

20
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,900
and milestones carry the dates the

21
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,640
customer was promised.

22
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:09,020
Engineering releases the general

23
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,080
arrangement drawing.

24
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,520
Revision two supersedes revision one,

25
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,260
and the order is linked to the exact

26
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:17,700
revision it is built from.

27
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,240
The bill of materials scales to the order,

28
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:23,480
and every line is copied onto it,

29
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,560
so a later change never rewrites work

30
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,940
already planned.

31
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,200
Before anything is cut,

32
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:34,040
Verity holds the stock the order needs.

33
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,940
One valve is short,

34
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:36,500
and it says so.

35
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,100
The purchase order is over the approval

36
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:42,160
limit, so it waits for a decision.

37
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,180
Two valves arrive, then the rest,

38
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,760
and the hold goes through.

39
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,300
On the floor, each team sees the stages

40
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,160
that are ready for them.

41
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:55,540
A stage cannot start until the one before

42
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:56,740
it is done.

43
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:00,780
Checks are measured,

44
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:03,060
with units and limits.

45
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,680
The pressure test finds a weeping flange.

46
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,020
The skid goes back to assembly,

47
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:10,040
and the failed result stays on record.

48
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:14,000
The retest passes. The photograph is taken

49
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,260
on a phone, and it belongs to this order,

50
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:17,680
and no other.

51
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:23,420
The test report leads with the summary.

52
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:25,420
Dispatch needs a packing photograph,

53
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:27,740
a vehicle, and a transporter.

54
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,640
Each skid carries a verification passport.

55
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:34,020
Scan it, and the customer sees what was

56
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,340
inspected, and nothing private.

57
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,380
Cost builds from the records themselves.

58
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:43,300
The approved quote,

59
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,760
the materials consumed,

60
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,720
the hours logged, the outside work.

61
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,400
Margin is worked out every time you look.

62
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,520
Invoices and payments are recorded against

63
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,280
the job, and one project file holds the

64
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,700
reports, the dispatch papers,

65
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,080
and the photographs.

66
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,440
Step back, and the operation reads on one

67
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,800
page. What is confirmed,

68
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,700
what is waiting, what is late,

69
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:10,860
what is on the floor,

70
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,560
and what is running short.

71
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,780
Every figure opens the record behind it.

72
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:21,360
Ask a question in plain language.

73
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:23,120
The assistant answers from the records

74
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,820
your role can open,

75
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,240
flags anything it could not confirm,

76
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,157
and asks before it acts.

77
00:03:33,057 --> 00:03:35,277
Every change is attributed.

78
00:03:35,277 --> 00:03:37,617
Releasing a drawing is its own permission.

79
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:40,017
And every record keeps its history.

80
00:03:43,617 --> 00:03:45,437
The questions still come.

81
00:03:45,437 --> 00:03:47,017
They just no longer all come to one

82
00:03:47,017 --> 00:03:48,097
person.

83
00:03:49,097 --> 00:03:51,777
People work from clear responsibilities,

84
00:03:51,777 --> 00:03:53,497
and leadership gets back to the decisions

85
00:03:53,497 --> 00:03:55,977
only leadership can make.

86
00:03:59,777 --> 00:04:01,957
Verity, for manufacturing.
